# SD:/etc/session/console -- the console session's programs: run by /bin/session (the autostart's line
# `session`) when SD:/etc/system.ini says "shell = console" (PocketUI's console mode: the games, a television,
# a pad), ended when the mode is switched to another (the Control Panel's Mode, `session switch`). The same
# syntax as SD:/etc/autostart. No menu bar, no dock: the menus are revealed on demand (PocketUI's phase P9).
#
# The console's home -- the library, the save states, the settings -- comes with phase P9
# (docs/POCKETUI-TECH-STUDY.md); it will be this file's line:
#   run consolehome
# Until then the Game Library stands in for it, the Terminal behind it (Alt+Tab: `session switch desktop`).
# The notifications: notifyd starts with the first one (SystemKit's notify).
run terminal
run gamelib
